    "# WGAN-GP on Fashion-MNIST (Option B)\n",
    "\n",
    "Adapted from the WGAN-GP notebook in David Foster, *Generative Deep Learning* (2nd ed.), O'Reilly, 2023, Chapter 4;\n",
    "code from [github.com/davidADSP/Generative_Deep_Learning_2nd_Edition](https://github.com/davidADSP/Generative_Deep_Learning_2nd_Edition)\n",
    "(`notebooks/04_gan/02_wgan_gp`).\n",
    "\n",
    "**Changes from Foster's notebook**\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Dataset:** Fashion-MNIST instead of CelebA, which the assignment allows. The 70,000 train+test images are loaded with `tf.keras.datasets.fashion_mnist`, resized from 28x28 to 64x64 and scaled to [-1, 1]. `CHANNELS = 1`.\n",
    "* **Data pipeline:** an in-memory `tf.data` pipeline with `.repeat()`, so it never runs out mid-training.\n",
    "* **Monitoring (new):** losses are logged after every epoch. Every `SAMPLE_EVERY` epochs the notebook saves a 5x5 grid from *fixed* latent vectors and measures **sample diversity** (mean pairwise L2 distance between 500 generated images, compared with the same number for 500 real images). That gives a number to check for mode collapse.\n",
    "* **Optional ablation:** the last section reruns training with one hyperparameter changed (for example `gp_weight=0`), for evidence of hyperparameter sensitivity.\n",
    "\n",
    "The architecture, optimizer settings, `CRITIC_STEPS = 3`, `GP_WEIGHT = 10` and batch size 512 follow Foster. As in Foster, one \"epoch\" is only `STEPS_PER_EPOCH = 2` generator updates, so the results are reported in **generator steps**.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Reproducing:** run all cells top to bottom. Everything is seeded with `SEED = 42`. GPU kernels are not bit-for-bit deterministic, so curves will differ slightly between runs. The environment and hardware are printed in the next cell, and the run settings are saved to `output/baseline/run_info.json`."
   ]
  },
